/*!
    \class vsmm::IGameMngr
    \inmodule VSMM
    \brief Interface of the game manager, declares the properties \l vsmm::GameMngr exposes to QML.

    IGameMngr is the abstract base of \l vsmm::GameMngr. It declares the
    installed game version, the extra mods folders, the disabled mods and a
    function that starts the game.

    \l vsmm::ModStore and \l vsmm::ModLoader take a pointer to this interface
    through their \c setGameMngr() functions, not to \l vsmm::GameMngr, so
    unit tests can pass a mock instead. \l vsmm::ModStore reloads the mods
    when \l modsDirsChanged() is emitted.

    The two properties and the invokable functions are what QML sees on the
    \c GameMngr singleton.

    \sa vsmm::GameMngr
*/

/*!
    \property vsmm::IGameMngr::gameVersion
    \brief The installed game version as a string, for example \c 1.21.0.

    The value is empty when the version is unknown. It is read with
    \l getGameVersionString() and changes are announced with
    \l gameVersionChanged().

    \sa getGameVersion()
*/

/*!
    \property vsmm::IGameMngr::disabledMods
    \brief Ids of the mods disabled in the game's \c clientsettings.json.

    The value is read with \l getDisabledModsQML() and changes are announced
    with \l disabledModsChanged().

    \sa getDisabledMods()
*/

/*!
    \fn vsmm::IGameMngr::~IGameMngr()
    Destroys the game manager.
*/

/*!
    \fn const QList<QDir> &vsmm::IGameMngr::getModsDirs() const
    Returns the mods folders listed in the game's client settings.

    \sa modsDirsChanged()
*/

/*!
    \fn const std::optional<semver::version<>> &vsmm::IGameMngr::getGameVersion() const
    Returns the installed game version, or an empty optional when the version
    is unknown.

    \sa getGameVersionString(), gameVersionChanged()
*/

/*!
    \fn QString vsmm::IGameMngr::getGameVersionString() const
    Returns the result of \l getGameVersion() formatted as a string, or an
    empty string when the version is unknown.

    This function is not virtual, so every implementation formats the version
    the same way. It is the READ accessor of the \l gameVersion property.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::IGameMngr::launchGame() const
    Starts the game. This function is invokable from QML.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::IGameMngr::addDisabledMod(const QString &modId, const QString &version)
    Disables the mod \a modId at \a version in the game's client settings.
    This function is invokable from QML.

    \sa removeDisabledMod(), disabledModsChanged()
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::IGameMngr::removeDisabledMod(const QString &modId)
    Enables the mod \a modId again by removing it from the disabled mods in
    the game's client settings. This function is invokable from QML.

    \sa addDisabledMod(), disabledModsChanged()
*/

/*!
    \fn const QSet<QString> &vsmm::IGameMngr::getDisabledMods() const
    Returns the ids of the disabled mods as a set.

    \sa getDisabledModsQML()
*/

/*!
    \fn QStringList vsmm::IGameMngr::getDisabledModsQML() const
    Returns the ids of the disabled mods as a list. It is the READ accessor
    of the \l disabledMods property.

    \sa getDisabledMods()
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::IGameMngr::modsDirsChanged()
    This signal is emitted when the mods should be reloaded, for example
    after the mods folders change. \l vsmm::ModStore reloads the mods when it
    receives it.

    \sa getModsDirs()
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::IGameMngr::disabledModsChanged()
    This signal is emitted when the set of disabled mod ids changes. It is
    the NOTIFY signal of the \l disabledMods property. \l vsmm::ModStore
    emits its \c modsChanged() signal on it, so its \c enabledModsCount
    property updates.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::IGameMngr::gameVersionChanged()
    This signal is emitted when the game version changes. It is the NOTIFY
    signal of the \l gameVersion property.
*/

/*!
    \class vsmm::GameMngr
    \inmodule VSMM
    \brief Reads the game version, mods folders and disabled mods, and launches the game.

    GameMngr is the implementation of \l vsmm::IGameMngr. It is a QML
    singleton named \c GameMngr. \l vsmm::App takes the instance from the
    QML engine and passes the settings to it with \l setConfig().

    The game version is read by running the executable from the
    \c gameExe path of \l vsmm::PathSettings with the \c --version argument
    and parsing its output as a semantic version. \l setConfig() does this
    once and waits up to three seconds for the result. When the \c gameExe
    path changes later, the version is read again without blocking, with the
    same three second limit. A \c gameExe change while a read is running is
    ignored with a warning. A process that does not exit in time is killed.
    When the read fails, the version becomes unknown.

    The mods folders and the disabled mods come from \c clientsettings.json in
    the \c gameConfig folder of \l vsmm::PathSettings. Only files with
    \c settingsVersion \c 1.16 are accepted. The file is read every time
    \l {vsmm::IConfig::gameConfigPathChanged()}{gameConfigPathChanged()} is
    emitted and every time the file changes on disk.
    A file that cannot be read on a change on disk leaves the current values
    as they are.

    \l {vsmm::IGameMngr::modsDirsChanged()}{modsDirsChanged()} is emitted when
    the mods folders change, every time
    \l {vsmm::IConfig::gameConfigPathChanged()}{gameConfigPathChanged()} is
    emitted, and
    when the game version changes after the mods folders were read once.
    While a version read is running, the signal waits until the read ends.
*/

/*!
    \fn vsmm::GameMngr::GameMngr()
    Constructs the game manager. Nothing is read until \l setConfig() is
    called.
*/

/*!
    \fn vsmm::GameMngr::~GameMngr()
    Destroys the game manager. A running version read process is killed.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::GameMngr::setConfig(vsmm::IConfig *config)
    Sets the settings to \a config and reads the game version.

    This function blocks for up to three seconds while the game executable
    prints its version. After this call, a change of the \c gameConfig path
    reads \c clientsettings.json again and a change of the \c gameExe path
    reads the version again.

    The settings can be set only once. A second call logs a warning and does
    nothing. A null \a config is a fatal error.

    \sa vsmm::IConfig
*/

/*!
    \fn const QList<QDir> &vsmm::GameMngr::getModsDirs() const
    \reimp
    Entries named \c Mods and empty entries of \c modPaths are skipped.
*/

/*!
    \fn const std::optional<semver::version<>> &vsmm::GameMngr::getGameVersion() const
    \reimp
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::GameMngr::launchGame() const
    \reimp
    Starts the \c gameExe executable as a detached process, with its own
    folder as the working directory.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::GameMngr::addDisabledMod(const QString &modId, const QString &version)
    \reimp
    Appends \c {modId@version} to \c disabledMods in \c clientsettings.json
    unless the same entry is already there.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::GameMngr::removeDisabledMod(const QString &modId)
    \reimp
    Removes every \c disabledMods entry with this mod id from
    \c clientsettings.json, whatever its version.
*/

/*!
    \fn const QSet<QString> &vsmm::GameMngr::getDisabledMods() const
    \reimp
*/

/*!
    \fn QStringList vsmm::GameMngr::getDisabledModsQML() const
    \reimp
*/

/*!
    \class vsmm::App
    \inmodule VSMM
    \brief The application, creates the QML engine and connects the backend singletons.

    App is the \c QGuiApplication subclass that \c main() creates. Its
    constructor does all of the startup work: it sets the application name,
    version and icon, handles the \c --help and \c --version command line
    options, and loads the QML user interface.

    The backend objects are QML singletons. App takes them from the QML
    engine and connects them to each other: \l vsmm::Config,
    \l vsmm::GameMngr, \l vsmm::ModStore, \l vsmm::ModLoader,
    \l vsmm::ModListModel, \l vsmm::ModSortFilterModel and
    \l vsmm::ModUpdateModel. It also owns the \l vsmm::HttpClient used by
    \l vsmm::ModLoader and by the \l vsmm::ModImageProvider registered as
    \c {image://modicon}.
*/

/*!
    \fn vsmm::App::App(int &argc, char *argv[])
    Constructs the application with the command line given by \a argc and
    \a argv.

    The constructor sets the Quick Controls style to \c VSMMStyle with
    \c Basic as the fallback, registers the \c modicon image provider and
    loads the \c Main QML component. It sets the \c IS_LINUX, \c IS_WINDOWS
    and \c IS_MACOS context properties for the current platform.

    It then passes the store, settings, game manager and HTTP client to the
    singletons that need them, and calls \c validate() on \l vsmm::Config,
    which makes \l vsmm::GameMngr read \c clientsettings.json when the
    \c gameConfig path points to an existing folder. A critical message is logged when the game
    version is unknown, because update detection is disabled then.

    A failure to create the QML root object is a fatal error.
*/

/*!
    \fn vsmm::App::~App()
    Destroys the application.
*/
